    "body": "Quick pass (coordinator, read only, no build) on head `67451c181`: the PR is a sub-PR of `side/path-kernel` and merges cleanly with it (`7f70d8b1a`). The author's checks are green on this head: `cargo check --tests` for pathkernel and motion, the `laws` suite (129 passed), the motion `kernel_laws` suite (29 passed), clippy, and the quick gate against the side branch (4 steps). The writer record on #4241 is released. The body starts with `Side branch: side/path-kernel` and has `Refs #4241`. The PR is flagged ready. It waits for the independent review.\n\nNotes for the reviewer:\n- The trial merge and the gate base are `origin/side/path-kernel`. The safety floor applies: the link proof decides where the tool stays down.\n- The PR does not reach the target of its issue. The lift counts for the material side Outside do not change (13 on the disc band, 15 on the dog-bone band, each with a named reason). The body says why. A follow-up issue has the next step.\n- The PR closes a safety gap: before it, a part that reaches out of the stock was inside the \"air\", and a stay-down link across that part was accepted. Check the pin `a_link_beside_a_part_that_reaches_out_of_the_stock_is_refused`.\n- The PR changes files outside `link/`: `region.rs` and `region_build.rs` (the part zone of an Outside region; the air leaves that zone out) and the visibility of the room definition of the entry stage. Check that the region pins of K1 and the entry pins of K5 still hold.\n- The light lane and the example catalog suites did not run. No old planner calls the new code.",
